assertion  XSH.iswblank.001
anchor     functions/iswblank.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswblank.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
since      2001
says       In the POSIX locale iswblank() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class blank as the locale definition lists it: the space and
           the tab.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswblank.002
anchor     functions/iswblank.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswblank.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
since      2001
says       In the POSIX locale iswblank() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the letters, digits, punctuation, the white-space characters
           other than space and tab (newline, vertical tab, form feed,
           carriage return), and the other controls.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswblank.003
anchor     functions/iswblank.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswblank.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       iswblank(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswblank.004
anchor     functions/iswblank.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswblank.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
since      2001
says       The two blank characters are also white-space characters:
           iswspace() is non-zero for them.
test       t/004-blank-is-space.c

assertion  XSH.iswblank.005
anchor     functions/iswblank.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswblank.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
since      2001
says       In a UTF-8 locale, iswblank() is still non-zero for the space and
           the tab.
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale (NOTINUSE otherwise);
           only ASCII-range characters are examined.
test       t/005-utf8-portable.c
